.TH "SPGEN-PUBLIC_API" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-public_api \- Generates the public API function for an operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.public_api [options] <COMMAND|QUERY>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The constituent's port: exactly one function per operation, nothing else.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the command or query the function stands for.
.SH "What the generator does"
One function per operation, its @spec typed as Architecture.public_api(…), and the body by what the operation does:
.IP \[bu] 2
create — generate the UUID, Map.put(params, "id", id), dispatch with consistency: :strong, return the projected read model.
.IP \[bu] 2
update — dispatch with the given id, return the read model.
.IP \[bu] 2
delete — dispatch, return :ok; no read model follows.
.IP \[bu] 2
read — the model's named query through Repo.one/1; nil → {:error, :not_found}. An oneOf id\-or\-slug parameter is realized once, in the query. The internal API is the port's after\-dispatch by_id lookup for create and update.
.IP \[bu] 2
collection — Repo.all over the query citizen (Queries.<Query>.new(query)). The port names the query, never the builder: which read model a collection reads and how a JSONAPI.Config becomes an Ecto query is the query's own contract (Query (./query.md)).
.PP
Validation errors surface through Sportipedia.Support.ErrorClassifier: Vex runs as commanded middleware, so there is no try/rescue and no param matching — both would swallow the error the caller needs.
.PP
What stays out of the port by design: anything that belongs to the internal API, and any function not named by the model.
.SH Tests
In the operation test (./operation\-test.md), under describe "Public API": success, {:error, {:validation_failure, _}} for commands, :not_found for a read of an unknown id, the unknown\-id and success cases for delete. The successful read (seed, then read) and the update cases are manual (Known gaps (../../README.md#known\-gaps)).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/public_api.ex (public function per operation)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>_test.exs (public function call tests)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none|read|collection (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.IP \(bu 2
read
.IP \(bu 2
collection
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND|QUERY\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
